       <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The IEEE 802.1 Working Group has specified Connectivity Fault
-Management (CFM) [802.1Q] OAM <xref target="RFC6291" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6291"/> facilities.  CFM messages are
+Management (CFM) <xref target="802.1Q" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="802.1Q"/> OAM <xref target="RFC6291" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6291"/> facilities.  CFM messages are
 structured with an OpCode field and have provision for the inclusion
 of TLV-structured information.</t>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">IEEE 802.1 has allocated the block of 32 CFM OpCodes from 64 through
 95 and the block of 32 CFM TLV Types from 64 through 95 to the IETF
-(see Appendix A).  This document specifies the IANA considerations
+(see <xref target="section-appendix.a" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Appendix A"/>).  This document specifies the IANA considerations
 for the assignment of values from these two blocks.</t>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">IEEE 802.1 previously allocated similar blocks of values from 32
 through 63 to ITU-T <xref target="Y.1731" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Y.1731"/>.</t>
